<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of South American</p>
<p>Libertadores Cup first round matches played Thursday:</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p>In Guayaquil, Ecuador: Emelec (Ecuador) 2 Racing Club</p>
<p>(Argentina) 2 (halftime 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Emelec - Ariel Graziani (26 and 68)</p>
<p>Racing Club - Ruben Capria (42), Fernando Queiroz (59)</p>
<p>Attendance - 45,000</p>
<p>Group three</p>
<p>In Santiago: Colo Colo (Chile) 1 Mineros (Venezuela) 0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Hector Tapia (22, penalty)</p>
<p>Group five</p>
<p>In Montevideo: Nacional (Uruguay) 1 Penarol (Uruguay) 4</p>
<p>(1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Nacional - Juan Ravera (24)</p>
<p>Penarol - Luis Romero (45), Pablo Bengoechea (60, penalty,</p>
<p>and 82, penalty), Marcelo Zalayeta (89)</p>
<p>    Standings			P  W  D  L  F  A  PTS</p>
<p>Grupo two</p>
<p>  Emelec			     2  1  1  0  4  3   4</p>
<p>  Nacional (Ecuador)	     2  1  0  1  2  2   3</p>
<p>  Velez Sarsfield (Argentina)  2  1  0  1  2  2   3</p>
<p>  Racing Club			2  0  1  1  3  4   1</p>
<p>Grupo three</p>
<p>  Universidad Catolica (Chile) 2  1  1  0  8  2   4</p>
<p>  Colo-Colo			  2  1  1  0  3  2   4</p>
<p>  Minerven (Venezuela)	   1  0  1  0  0  0   1</p>
<p>  Mineros			    3  0  1  2  0  7   1</p>
<p>Grupo 5</p>
